    sources: ["cidr", "global"],
    advanced: "Historical classes assigned A, B, and C different default network sizes; class D described multicast and class E reserved space. Modern routing uses longest-prefix matching with explicit CIDR lengths. Aggregation trades table detail for responsibility over larger coverage.",
