    steps: ["Ping commonly sends ICMP Echo Requests and measures received Echo Replies.", "Traceroute sends probes with increasing TTL values.", "A forwarding router that exhausts TTL may return ICMP Time Exceeded, revealing a responder address.", "UDP traceroute commonly ends with destination port-unreachable; ICMP variants use Echo, and TCP variants probe a selected TCP port.", "Interpret unanswered probes cautiously because filtering, rate limits, return-path loss, or different probe treatment can hide responders."],
    example: { given: "Three probes use TTL 1, 2, and 3. Replies come from R1, R2, and then the destination.", result: "The probes exposed a two-router forward path under those probe conditions.", steps: ["TTL 1 expires at R1.", "TTL 2 survives R1 and expires at R2.", "TTL 3 reaches the destination.", "Each reply takes its own return route.", "The observed round-trip times include both directions and processing, so subtracting adjacent hop times is not a reliable link-delay measurement."] },
