    observe: "Compare ping, destination-port tests, and route traces using the same target. Record probe type and time; changing load-balanced paths can alter the result.",
    interview: { answer: "ICMP reports selected network conditions. Ping tests Echo response; traceroute exploits hop lifetime and feedback. Filtering and path asymmetry limit what either can prove.", followups: ["Why can TCP traceroute differ from UDP traceroute?", "Why are hop RTT differences misleading?"] },
