    example: { given: "An Ethernet neighbor has IPv6 address 2001:db8::ab:1234 and no cached MAC.", result: "Its solicited-node multicast address is ff02::1:ffab:1234.", steps: ["Take the target's low 24 bits: ab:1234.", "Append those bits to ff02::1:ff00:0/104.", "Send a solicitation to ff02::1:ffab:1234, commonly mapped to Ethernet 33:33:ff:ab:12:34.", "The target advertises its link address.", "Cache the mapping and send the waiting packet. This multicast group narrows recipients but need not uniquely identify one address."] },
    failure: "Blocking all ICMPv6 can prevent address resolution, router discovery, and size feedback while ordinary application rules appear correct.",
